      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">LEGAL COMPLIANCE</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Transportation Rangareddy 8409531615</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">
	<p>When transporting a car within Rangareddy or to another location, certain documents are required to ensure a smooth and secure process. Below is a list of essential paperwork:</p>

	<p>To transport your car, you need a valid copy of the Registration Certificate (RC). This copy should be self-attested, meaning you must affix your signature or seal it before submitting it. This document is essential for identification purposes and ensures that the car being transported belongs to you.</p>

	<p>Provisional Pollution Control Certificate (PUC) is another important document required for car transportation. PUC verifies that your car meets environmental standards and is in a good condition for road usage. Ensure that your PUC is up-to-date before initiating the transportation process.</p>

	<p>A valid insurance certificate is necessary to cover your car during transportation. The insurance policy should cover damages or losses incurred during transit. Ensure that your insurance certificate has not expired and provides adequate coverage for the journey.</p>

	<p>Before transporting your car, it is essential to obtain an IBA-approved consignment bill of lading. This document serves as a contract between you and the transportation company, outlining the terms and conditions of the service, including the car's condition, destination, and insurance details.</p>

	<p>A declaration affidavit is crucial to ensure that you declare the full value of your car to the transportation company. This declaration confirms that you are aware of the risks associated with car transportation and fully understand the insurance coverage provided.</p>

	<p>Before the transportation process begins, a vehicle condition report should be prepared. This document details the current condition of your car, including its overall condition, mileage, and any existing damages. This report serves as a reference point for comparison after transportation.</p>

	<p>To ensure the safe transportation of your car, a vehicle identity document is necessary. This document should have all the necessary information about your car, including the make, model, year, and registration details.</p>

	<p>A detailed description of your car, including specifications such as engine type, engine capacity, transmission type, and chassis number, is essential for a smooth transportation process. This information helps the transportation company ensure secure and accurate handling of your vehicle.</p>

	<p>A consignment note is a crucial document that outlines the details of your car, including the make, model, color, and any damages or defects. This note serves as a reference point for comparison after transportation.</p>

	<p>The bill of lading is a formal agreement between you and the transportation company. It outlines the terms and conditions of the transportation service, including the pick-up and delivery locations, transportation mode, and insurance details.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



